The independent reviews converged on two root causes: fixed remainder capture and nominal escrow insolvency after a negative rebase. Function isolation makes the latter two findings (`release` and `claim`). One additional reviewer proved an uncapped ERC-20 hook can exhaust the payout loop’s gas; I’m retaining it after tracing the EIP-150 gas path.
